{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/888813-if-supers-came-to-our-world-which-would-have-it-easier","id":888813,"title":"If supers came to our world, which would have it easier?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-11T20:52:25-07:00","id":888813,"title":"If supers came to our world, which would have it easier?","content":"Let's say some weird wormhole opened up in the world of darkness version of Earth and sucked a few hundred members of one of the various supernatural groups over (Fera, vamps, mages, Changlings etc).. Which one of them do you think would have it easier adapting to OUR world?<br /> Which would WE accept more? Which would we accept less??<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:02:59-07:00","id":888836,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of them would really be accepted.<br /> <br /> But as for those who would be able to fit in fine, there's Wraiths, vampires from Requiem, the Uratha, Demons from Descent. Possibly Mummies from the Resurrection.<br /> <br /> I'm only qualifying the Requiem vampires from the Masquerade ones because the Camarilla and Sabbat wouldn't really be adaptable to our world, it would require hundreds of years of groundwork, while Requiem vampires are less grandiose in scheme. If you could get past the internecine warfare, world domination and Jyhadism, Masquerade vampires could probably adapt well too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:46:30-07:00","id":888856,"title":"","content":"Depends on your definition of accepted. Vampires? A secret to immortality is one that is most definitely going to be pursued, but it in the possession of bloodsucking monsters is a terrifying concept - they would be accepted, likely in the same way you accept a dangerous animal; No where near the level of worth that a person has, something to study, and something to put down if it proves too dangerous.<br /> <br /> Wraiths and ghosts would fit in fine and be... about as accepted as they are now? Definitive proof would most certainly change the world view, but you'd still get people thinking it was all a hoax.<br /> <br /> Mages... BURN THE WITCH. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Nah they'd be fine. We accept 'mages' of owod now (well... as a collective. Individuals on the other hand...) - in that case it'd be more about the exposure of magic than anything else. I like to think that these days this would be accepted, but I know more than a few cultures that would be getting out their pitchforks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:30:55-07:00","id":889322,"title":"","content":"True, how one defines accepted can matter a lot.. I was more on about which would seem to be LESS likely to get the entire populus on their butts, much like in darn near EVERY Tv show/film where superpowered individuals show up, some govt agency either wants them dead OR working exclusively for the govt..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:59:31-07:00","id":889677,"title":"","content":"My first question is, how long before we acknowledge that they truly exist? One thing Lestat got right is that mankind just wouldn't *believe* in the supernatural, even with clear evidence. Really making people believe on a mass, public scale would require some massive public event...while most supernaturals have spent centuries building cultures that avoid such spectacle. <br /> <br /> They are most likely to think that, even without real supernatural influence in our history, they are better off going underground and continuing their various masquerades, as humanity isn't THAT different...and for all they know, there *are* supernaturals native to this world, but they are just hiding very well.<br /> <br /> So, I don't see them becoming well-known, and eventually this becomes the WoD. Playing Devil's Advocate, however, and assuming they are exposed for some reason...lots of people will be excited by the idea, esp those with romantic notions of beautiful yet tormented monsters, but will probably change their minds as soon as they meet one. <br /> <br /> Most of the supers could eventually be accepted, were it not for the fact that almost all have some sort of &quot;frenzy&quot; condition that makes them lose control and lash out at the world around them. Even those with minor conditions will be tainted by those with major ones, and humanity as a whole will soon lose all tolerance. Perhaps needless to say, but Prometheans will be the first up against the wall...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:02:13-07:00","id":891389,"title":"","content":"We don't really accept monsters in our world. And Monsters don't want to be exposed. That being said.<br /> Those denizens that could adapt to our world are the same creatures that could play low key and out of view.<br /> Those denizens whos supernatural abilities are covered up. A number of splats have a Quiescence/ Lunacy characteristic. Then its just a question of not getting on the wrong side of law.<br /> <br /> So I'd say that vamps have the least problems, because they already play the masquerade game.<br /> Mage have a few problems, that of being a new person without ID. But they have a few tricks to help them out.<br /> Urtha have the problem of abandoning their old lives and the rage monster inside. They have the lunacy mechanic but people just don't forget rage events. anything that leaves causalities is going to be looked at.<br /> Changeling have similar problems to Urtha of new person, but without the rage monsters issues","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:25:42-07:00","id":891675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/888813-if-supers-came-to-our-world-which-would-have-it-easier?p=891389#post891389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't really accept monsters in our world</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly you've never been to Seattle.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:21:15-07:00","id":893416,"title":"","content":"Answer: none of them as those creatures clearly come from a reality where the laws of reality are different. The vampires would drop down as dead bodies, the wraiths would fade into nothingness and the rest would be cut off from their various supernatural powers and homelands. Most would end up in mental institutions for their delusions, morgues as suicides or failed attempts at executing their powers, and imprisoned or destitute for lack of a properly established identity. A few of the cleverer, quicker and luckier ones might avoid these fates, but I think they would be in increasingly small numbers as time passes.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know, I just gave a Banal enough answer to kill a faerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:08:59-07:00","id":893762,"title":"","content":"I think vampire would be the most accepted, I think that there is enough vampire lover, and fanboy and emo and goth and all the &quot;real vampire&quot; fad going on, that would actually jump on the first chance they would get to become true vampire, even if it actually meant drinking blood from other people. Even more so if they actually have access to all their power and strength in the real world. That would make them Super heroes or Villain, depending on their nature and personality. I sure many would fear them, and depending on how to arrive, I am sure the army and government would try to covert all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}